WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.522 --> 00:00:02.492
Here is a customer asking for an appointment.

2
00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:07.451
The workflow checks the request and calendar before it confirms anything.

3
00:00:11.008 --> 00:00:18.821
When the time is available, the demo creates one booking and returns its reference, so the customer knows it is confirmed.

4
00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:28.272
If the same request arrives again, it returns the existing reference instead of booking twice.

5
00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.242
The booking count stays at one.

6
00:00:33.508 --> 00:00:40.940
If the calendar is unavailable, it clearly says the appointment is not confirmed and leaves the request for follow-up.

7
00:00:44.063 --> 00:00:49.715
For your setup, I would connect the enquiry channel, Claude and calendar through n eight n.

8
00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:55.068
This tested prototype uses sample data and simulated integrations.
